# P5a (appended): the Spectral engine's parameters for each slot: the resynthesis of a sample from its analysis (partials and noise). The sample is
# the slot's "A sample" (built-in or User) and "A root" is the note it sounds at its own pitch; "A position" is where the reading starts (and, at
# speed 0, where it holds); "A loop", "A loop start", "A loop end" and "A reverse" apply as for the Sample engine. Tuning, level, pan, unison,
# detune and spread are the slot's own. The resynthesis takes no warps.
group Osc A
ASpSpeed   "A spectral speed" 0 1000 250 lin 0 400 % 0 | Spectral engine: how fast the sample is read, as a share of its own speed, without changing its pitch (100 %: as recorded, 25 %: four times slower, 0: frozen at "A position")
    how Sets how fast the model of the sample is read, from frozen at 0 % through as recorded at 100 % to four times faster at 400 %.
    sound Slower reads stretch the sound out without lowering it; 0 % holds one moment of it as a steady drone; faster reads squeeze it.
ASpKey     "A key tracking" 0 1000 1000 pct | Spectral engine: how much the pitch follows the key played (100 %: the sample sounds at its own pitch on its root note and moves with the keys; 0: every key sounds the sample's own pitch)
    how Sets how far the pitch follows the played key, from every key at the sample's own pitch at 0 % to a full semitone per key at 100 %.
    sound At 100 % the sample plays as a melody instrument; lower values make the keys change less than a semitone each, and at 0 % they only retrigger it.
ASpFormant "A formant keep" 0 1000 0 pct | Spectral engine: holds the sample's spectral envelope (its vowel or body colour) in place when the pitch changes, so that a shifted voice does not turn into a chipmunk or a giant
    how Sets how much of the sample's spectral envelope stays where it was when the pitch is shifted, instead of moving with the partials.
    sound At 100 % a voice pitched up keeps its vowel and size; at 0 % the whole timbre moves with the pitch, as in a sped-up recording.
ASpSnap    "A harmonic snap" 0 1000 0 pct | Spectral engine: pulls each partial toward the nearest multiple of the sample's fundamental (100 %: all partials exactly harmonic; frames without a clear pitch are left alone)
    how Sets how far each partial is pulled to the nearest whole multiple of the sample's fundamental, from untouched at 0 % to exactly harmonic at 100 %.
    sound Snapping cleans a rough or slightly out-of-tune tone into a pure one and takes the beating out of inharmonic partials.
ASpBalance "A tonal noise" 0 1000 500 pct | Spectral engine: the balance of the two halves of the model: 0 is the noise only, 50 % both as analysed, 100 % the partials only
    how Sets the balance between the sample's noise and its partials: 0 % plays only the noise, 50 % both as recorded, 100 % only the partials.
    sound Toward 100 % the sound becomes clean and pitched; toward 0 % it turns into a breathy, pitchless wash that keeps the sample's colour.
ASpBlur    "A blur" 0 1000 0 pct | Spectral engine: smooths the model over time (up to 300 ms either side), so that attacks and changes are spread out and drift into each other
    how Sets how far in time the model is smoothed, from exact at 0 % to blurred over about a third of a second at 100 %.
    sound Higher values soften attacks and slur changes together into a smeared, dreamy texture.
ASpPartials "A spectral partials" 1 64 48 int 0 | Spectral engine: how many partials sound (the model keeps up to 64 a frame, roughly loudest first); each added partial costs CPU
    how Sets how many of the sample's partials are played, from the first one to all 64 the model can hold.
    sound Fewer partials sound thinner and simpler; they cost less CPU, and the noise keeps the missing body.
ASpTilt    "A spectral tilt" 0 1000 500 lin -24 24 dB/oct 1 | Spectral engine: brightness; each octave above the middle of the sample's spectrum louder (+) or softer (-) by this many dB
    how Sets the slope of the partials' levels around the middle of the spectrum, in dB per octave, from darker at negative values to brighter at positive ones.
    sound Positive values make the sound brighter and thinner; negative values make it darker and rounder.
ASpStretch "A spectral stretch" 0 1000 500 lin -100 100 % 0 | Spectral engine: spreads the partials from whole multiples of the fundamental: + stretches them apart (bells, glass), - bunches them
    how Sets how far the partials are spread from the whole multiples of the fundamental, from bunched together at negative values to stretched apart at positive ones.
    sound Stretching turns a tone into something bell-like or metallic; bunching it makes it dense and clustered.

